# Interactive help
HIcon:This is the SSH server. Click SELECT to open its log, ADJUST for the authorized keys, MENU for the settings and more.
HLog:The server's log, newest line at the bottom; also written to the file log in SSHd's Choices directory.
HInfo:Information about this copy of SSHd.
HInput:Type or paste a public key here (the content of an id_*.pub file), then press RETURN or click Add.
HAdd:Click SELECT to add the key in the field to the authorized keys.
HAccount:The account on another machine whose public keys you want to allow, as user@host or user@host:port.
HPassword:That account's password. It is used once to log in and read its id_ed25519, id_ecdsa and id_rsa public keys, then forgotten.
HImport:Click SELECT to log in to the machine named on the left and import its public keys.
HHost:This server's host key fingerprint. On your first connection ssh prints the same text; answer yes only if they match.
HDelete:Click SELECT to remove this key; it will no longer be able to log in.
HDrop:Drop a file containing public keys anywhere on this window to add them.
HMInfo:Move right to see information about this version of SSHd.
HMHelp:Click SELECT to read the help for SSHd.
HMLog:Click SELECT to open the log window, which follows the server's activity.
HMVerbose:Click SELECT to turn detailed logging on or off. This lasts until SSHd quits; set 'verbose' in Choices to keep it.
HMKeys:Click SELECT to open the window of keys that may log in.
HMChoices:Click SELECT to edit the settings in your text editor; they apply when SSHd is next started.
HMQuit:Click SELECT to stop the SSH server and remove it from the icon bar.
HLMOpen:Click SELECT to open the log file in your text editor, to read, search or copy it.
HLMClear:Click SELECT to empty this window; the log file keeps every line.
